\f1\fs22 As the sun sets, the crowd of Elvis impersonators forms a dense circle like a colorful, rhinestone-studded galaxy. They stand in their full regalia, sporting pompadours that range from jet black to platinum blond, each meticulously styled with a dash of rebellious flair. Their sideburns are thick and daring, their faces a canvas of carefully applied '70s stage makeup - eyes rimmed with kohl and lips painted a glossy, vibrant pink, the color of youth and defiance.\
\
The air shimmers with a confetti of sequins from their glistening jumpsuits, every hue of the rainbow present. Some are pure white, others flaming red, midnight black, and electric blue. Each one is adorned with an array of rhinestones that twinkle as they catch the dying light, an army of mini constellations. The impersonators' bell-bottomed silhouettes are punctuated by glossy patent leather shoes, as polished as their performances.\
\
They stand shoulder to shoulder, their eyes fixed on the speaker at the center of their circle, one of their own. This Elvis holds the crowd in rapt attention, his voice a booming baritone echoing off the nearby buildings. His hands gesticulate with the natural charisma of a born performer, while his eyes, intense and filled with the spirit of the King himself, meet the gazes of his bedazzled brethren.\
\
Even amidst this sea of impersonators, they're individuals - some younger, others older, a few with the paunch of later Elvis years, some with the slim hips of his early days. Each bears the essence of Elvis in their own way, their expressions serious as they listen, their heads nodding in agreement or their faces creasing in laughter at the speaker's well-timed jokes. In the midst of the spectacle, there's a sense of camaraderie, a shared love for the King that transcends their individuality and unites them as a glittering, vibrant community.\
\
\
\
\
\'85 they were a pack of rhinestone-studded wolves, circling around a fire of shared admiration. Their heads were crowned with pompadours, ranging from the blackest raven to the platinum of a 1950's screen siren, each coiffed with a rebellious zeal that Elvis himself would have tipped his hat to.\
\
\'85 a lively parade of sequined jumpsuits, shimmering like a disco ball caught in a cyclone. Colors? Oh, they had colors. Some were as white as a dove, others as red as a flushed cheek, a few as dark as a moonless night, and a handful as blue as a summer sky. Each suit was studded with twinkling rhinestones that winked at the waning light, as if they held a secret the sun wasn't privy to. And the shoes, my, the shoes! Glossy and black, they were mirrors reflecting the audacity of their mission.\
\
In the center of this human kaleidoscope stood their speaker. He held their attention as if it were a hot poker, his voice booming with a baritone that bounced off the nearby buildings, resonating in their Elvis-loving hearts. His hands were as expressive as a Shakespearean actor's, while his eyes, carrying the spark of the King himself, pierced through each impersonator, instilling them with an Elvis-strength courage.\
\
Amongst the sequined sea of Elvises, each one was a unique note in this rock 'n' roll symphony. Some were youthful, lean and hip-swiveling, while others embraced the more mature, burger-loving Elvis. Each absorbed the speaker's words like a sponge, their heads bobbing in approval or their faces crinkling into laughter at a well-delivered joke. In this shimmering spectacle, there was a sense of unity, a shared rhythm that pulsed through them, binding them into a tribe that was as dazzling as it was devoted.
